              2
              SeNPs can efficiently convert near‐infrared (NIR) light into heat and exhibit excellent thermostability. In vitro experiments showed that CS‐Cu
              2
              SeNPs had selective cellular uptake between cancer and normal cells and expressed clear anticancer activity on A375 and HeLa human cancer cells. In addition, the anticancer activity was increased to about 400 \% by combination with a laser at 808 nm, which acted through induction of apoptosis with the involvement of intrinsic and extrinsic pathways. CS‐Cu
